title: pre-#68 bare-date 'started' stamps precede their own card
updated: 2026-08-12T01:17:23Z
---

Found while implementing `karr metrics` (#126), by running it against karr's own board.

karr stamped `started` as a bare date (YYYY-MM-DD) until ticket #68 made it a
full timestamp. A bare date reads as midnight UTC, so every ticket that was
filed and picked up on the same day now carries a `started` that is EARLIER
than its own `created` -- by up to a day. On this board: 75 of the 116
finished tickets, plus 18 more that are not finished.

Consequences seen so far:

- `karr metrics` had to exclude those cards from cycle time and flow
  efficiency; counting them made the average cycle time exceed the average
  lead time and reported a flow efficiency of 107.3%. The command now counts
  them in `unusable_timestamps` and says so, so 75 of 116 finished cards
  contribute no cycle time -- correct, but a large hole in the history.
- Anything else that ever subtracts `started` from `created` inherits the
  same trap, and there is nothing on the card that marks the stamp as
  day-granular.

What needs deciding (not by the metrics command):

- whether to migrate those stamps at all, and to what -- clamping `started`
  to `created` is the only defensible value (the work cannot have begun
  before the card existed) but it also asserts zero queue time, which is
  false for a card filed in the morning and picked up at night;
- whether that belongs in `karr repair` (today only about double-encoded
  UTF-8), in a normalization on read in Task.pm, or nowhere at all;
- whether a card whose `started` was only ever day-granular should be
  distinguishable from one stamped to the second.

Storage/migration side is karr-ref-worker territory; the read-side decision
touches Task.pm. Filed so the next reader of `started` does not rediscover
this the hard way.
Implemented in lib/App/karr/Cmd/Repair.pm: 'started' is raised to 'created' where a bare-date stamp precedes it. Criterion is narrow on purpose (bare-date started + karr-shaped created only); a full-timestamp start before creation is reported, not clamped. Regression test t/139-repair-started-clamp.t. Dry run on this board: 75 cards, 42 of which get a 'completed' before the new 'started' -- follow-ups #139 (the same bare-date bug in 'completed') and #140 (metrics' start guard stops guarding after the clamp).
